---
system: sys-01-identity-household-access
flow_id: household-invite-parent
surface: mobile
spec_anchor: /software/systems/01-identity-household-access#household-invite-adr-0010
actors: [ParentApp, Gateway, IdentityService, SES, PostgreSQL]
apis:
  - POST /v1/household/parents/invite
  - POST /v1/household/parents/accept
  - DELETE /v1/household/parents/{user_id}
externals: [SES]
queues: []
failure_paths:
  - not_primary_parent_role
  - email_already_household_member
  - invite_expired_7d
  - revoke_self_forbidden
  - last_secondary_warning
idempotency: invite dedup on (household_id, email_hash) — re-invite to same email within 7d reuses existing pending row
retry: single retry on 5xx
timeout: 3s
status: final
---
%% HAND-CURATED. UC-PR09 invite + UC-PR10 revoke per ADR-0010 D3. Primary issues invite (role=owner required). household_members table uses roles owner/manager/viewer; ADR "secondary_parent" maps to manager. Revoke sets status=revoked + revokes secondary's parent_sessions.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant ParentApp
    participant Gateway
    participant IdentityService
    participant SES
    participant PostgreSQL

    Note over ParentApp,IdentityService: UC-PR09 — Primary parent invites secondary (ADR-0010 D3)

    ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/household/parents/invite {email, nickname} + Bearer JWT (primary)
    Gateway->>Gateway: validate parent JWT — extract user_id, household_id
    Gateway->>IdentityService: forward request
    IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT role FROM household_members WHERE user_id={user_id} AND household_id={household_id}
    PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: role
    alt not_primary_parent_role (role != 'owner')
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 403 not_primary_parent_role {requires_role: 'owner'}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 403
    else primary_confirmed
        IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT id FROM users WHERE email={email}
        PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: invitee_user row or null
        IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT id FROM household_members WHERE household_id={household_id} AND email_hash=sha256({email}) AND status IN ('active','pending_invite')
        PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: existing member row or null
        alt email_already_household_member
            IdentityService-->>Gateway: 409 email_already_household_member
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 409
        else dedup — pending invite exists within 7d
            Note over IdentityService: Return existing invite — no new SES send
            IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {invite_id: existing, status: 'pending_invite', resent: false}
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
        else new_invite
            IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: INSERT household_members {id: uuid(), household_id, email_hash: sha256(email), nickname, role: 'manager', status: 'pending_invite', invited_by_user_id: user_id, invited_at: now(), expires_at: now()+7days}
            PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: invite_id
            IdentityService-)SES: (async) email magic link tbot://household/accept?token={invite_token} to {email}
            IdentityService-->>Gateway: 201 {invite_id, status: 'pending_invite', expires_at: now()+7days}
            Gateway-->>ParentApp: 201
        end
    end

    Note over ParentApp,IdentityService: UC-PR09 — Invitee accepts (ADR-0010 D3)

    ParentApp->>Gateway: POST /v1/household/parents/accept {token} + Bearer JWT (invitee)
    Gateway->>Gateway: validate invitee JWT — extract invitee user_id
    Gateway->>IdentityService: forward request
    IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT id, household_id, expires_at, status FROM household_members WHERE token_hash=sha256({token})
    PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: invite row or null
    alt token_not_found
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 404 invite_token_not_found
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 404
    else invite_expired_7d (expires_at <= now())
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 410 invite_expired_7d
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 410
    else invite_already_accepted (status = 'active')
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {status: 'active', already_member: true}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    else accept_invite
        IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE household_members SET status='active', user_id={invitee.user_id}, accepted_at=now() WHERE id={invite.id}
        PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: updated
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {status: 'active', household_id}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    end

    Note over ParentApp,IdentityService: UC-PR10 — Primary revokes secondary (ADR-0010 D5)

    ParentApp->>Gateway: DELETE /v1/household/parents/{target_user_id} + Bearer JWT (primary)
    Gateway->>Gateway: validate primary JWT
    Gateway->>IdentityService: forward request
    IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT role FROM household_members WHERE user_id={user_id} AND household_id={household_id}
    PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: caller role
    alt not_primary_parent_role
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 403 not_primary_parent_role
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 403
    else revoke_self_forbidden (target_user_id = user_id)
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 400 revoke_self_forbidden
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 400
    else revoke_secondary
        IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: SELECT COUNT(*) FROM household_members WHERE household_id={household_id} AND role='manager' AND status='active'
        PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: secondary_count
        IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE household_members SET status='revoked', revoked_at=now() WHERE user_id={target_user_id} AND household_id={household_id}
        PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: updated
        IdentityService->>PostgreSQL: UPDATE parent_sessions SET revoked_at=now() WHERE user_id={target_user_id} AND revoked_at IS NULL
        PostgreSQL-->>IdentityService: sessions revoked
        IdentityService-->>Gateway: 200 {revoked: true, last_secondary_warning: secondary_count = 1}
        Gateway-->>ParentApp: 200
    end

    Note over ParentApp,PostgreSQL: timeout 3s — invite dedup on (household_id, email_hash) — invite expires 7d — revoke revokes all target parent_sessions
